{"availability":"available","full":"caltechlibrary/waystation","name":"waystation","description":"Automatically archive your repository's GitHub Pages in the Wayback Machine.","category":"Other","language":"Makefile","stars":27,"forks":2,"created":"2022-11-09T20:20:34Z","updated":"2024-01-30T02:16:37Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://caltechlibrary.github.io/waystation","topics":["archiving","automation","documentation","github-action","github-actions","github-automation","github-pages","internet-archive","preservation","wayback-machine"],"demo":"https://caltechlibrary.github.io/waystation","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T02:04:34.789Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T02:04:34.789Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T02:04:34.789Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T02:04:34.789Z","stars":27,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Waystation is a GitHub Action that makes it easy to archive your repository's GitHub Pages site automatically in the Internet Archive's Wayback Machine.","Many projects use GitHub Pages for documentation and other purposes. GitHub Pages are wonderful, but they are not archived. To help ensure long-term access to your GitHub Pages, you may want to preserve them in the Internet Archive's Wayback Machine. That's the purpose of this GitHub Action.","GitHub is incredibly popular today, but the content is not guaranteed to be permanent; moreover, GitHub has in the past changed the URLs and policies surrounding GitHub Pages—and may do so again in the future. The Wayback Machine is a free digital archive of the World Wide Web founded by the Internet Archive. Web pages saved in the Wayback Machine continue to exist even after the original project repository changes or is removed from the web, and the archived pages can be searched for, shared, and linked to normally. You can also view previous versions of a site if they were archived."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https:/